{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VjmjXkL7CdwBtvknqsdovV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SthaqyassRMqSHkSxf18kG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/allocation_analysis.txt << 'EOF'\n# WHIR Memory Allocation Analysis\n\n## VPMM Page Size Change Impact\nChanged from 2MB (1x granularity) to 16MB (8x granularity) in commit 4863c316.\n\n### Allocation Threshold Behavior\nBefore: All allocations >= 2MB go through VPMM (cuMemCreate overhead)\nAfter: Only allocations >= 16MB go through VPMM; smaller ones use cudaMallocAsync\n\n### Allocations in Typical WHIR Proving (from whir.rs)\nAssuming m=16, k_whir=2, height=2^16=65536, D_EF=4:\n\n1. f_ple_evals: height * D_EF * sizeof(F) = 65536 * 4 * 8 bytes = 2.1 MB\n   - BEFORE: VPMM path (cuMemCreate cost)\n   - AFTER: cudaMallocAsync path (no page tracking)\n\n2. w_moments: (2^m) * sizeof(EF) = 65536 * 32 bytes = 2.1 MB\n   - BEFORE: VPMM path\n   - AFTER: cudaMallocAsync path\n\n3. g_rs (per round): D_EF * codeword_height * sizeof(F)\n   - For round 0: 4 * (2^16) * 8 bytes = 2.1 MB\n   - BEFORE: VPMM path\n   - AFTER: cudaMallocAsync path\n\n4. d_sumcheck_tmp (per round): variable based on tmp_buffer_capacity\n   - Typically 256K-512K elements = 8-16 MB\n   - Might cross the threshold\n\n5. d_z0_pows2, d_z_pows2: small vectors (log_height * num_queries elements)\n   - << 16 MB, always use cudaMallocAsync\n\n## Key Issue: Repeated Allocation/Deallocation Pattern\nIn WHIR sumcheck rounds (lines 215-219):\n- new_f_coeffs: output_height * sizeof(EF)\n- new_w_moments: output_height * sizeof(EF)\n- These are re-created in EACH sumcheck round within a WHIR round\n\nIf k_whir=2:\n- Round 0: create buffers for height 2^(m-0) -> 2^(m-1)\n- Round 1: create buffers for height 2^(m-1) -> 2^(m-2)\n\nWith 16MB threshold + cudaMallocAsync pooling, behavior changes:\n- cudaMallocAsync has its own memory pool management\n- Repeated small allocations may cause pool fragmentation/overhead\n- VPMM defragmentation doesn't occur for cudaMallocAsync allocations\n- cudaFreeAsync is stream-ordered, not synchronized\nEOF\ncat /tmp/allocation_analysis.txt\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":59510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2024,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsFWvH1ZUbtcR8rKDCrN4x","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"62c4d0dc-c63f-4469-92c8-e6883a36d008"}
