ride; threads beyond `query_stride` initialize to zero (line 30)\n\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/bn254_poseidon2.cu` (lines 183-268):\n  - Similar kernels for BN254\n  - Line 198 & 244: `Bn254Fr digest = bn254_zero_init();` for padding\n  - Uses `bn254_zero_init()` helper (lines 84-88) to initialize zero digests\n\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs` (lines 30-87):\n  - `GpuMerkleHash` trait with `compress_rows` and `compress_rows_ext` methods\n  - Routes to `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes` FFI (lines 121-148)\n\n### 3. **What `calculate_zero_hash` Likely Is**\n\nThe profiler kernel name `calculate_zero_hash` is most likely:\n- **A compiler-optimized inline kernel** generated from the row hashing logic for the case where `stride_idx >= query_stride`\n- OR a **separate code path compiled for zero-row processing** that the Nsight profiler has named\n- OR an **artifact of kernel name demangling** in the profiler output that doesn't match source symbol names\n\nThe actual GPU code initializes zero digests inline within the row hashing kernel, not in a separate kernel.\n\n### 4. **Frequency Per Proving Run**\n\nBased on the structure:\n- **Once per matrix per proving run** (called from `MerkleTreeGpu::new_generic_with_hash`)\n- **Per-AIR**: Each AIR being proven gets its own merkle tree built once\n- **Per-segment**: Not per segment; per-codeword matrix after RS encoding\n- Per the profiler: **584 instances total** in the profile run (likely 584 padding rows across all matrices)\n\n### 5. **Inputs & Precomputation**\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `digest_t *out` - output buffer for digests\n- `unsigned long` - likely output size (number of padding rows to hash)\n\n**Could they be precomputed?**\n- **NO** - The zero row hash is deterministic but must be computed once per matrix because:\n  - It depends on the width of the matrix (how many zero elements to hash)\n  - Different matrices may have different widths\n  - Must 