{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UX3gnJjnGy7SVjtvJj2v8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XRePeqPXuQZLd2i1MQTL8b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/kernel_details.txt << 'EOF'\n# WHIR CUDA Kernels & Operations\n\n## Core Kernels (whir.cu, lines 1-310)\n\n### 1. whir_algebraic_batch_traces_kernel (lines 24-74)\n   - Grid/Block: kernel_launch_params(stacked_height) - 1D grid\n   - Operation: Algebraically batch unstacked traces into one column vector\n   - Input: BatchingTracePacket array, mu_powers, skip_domain\n   - Algorithm:\n     * For each thread (row in stacked matrix):\n       - Iterate over all packets (traces)\n       - Compute stacked row offset accounting for skip_domain striding\n       - Accumulate: res += mu_pow[offset] * trace_val\n       - Store result in output (4 elements per stacked row = D_EF components)\n   - No shared memory usage, highly memory-bandwidth dependent\n\n### 2. whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round_kernel (lines 83-136)\n   - Grid/Block: kernel_launch_params(height >> 1, 256) - 1D grid of blocks\n   - Operation: Compute WHIR sumcheck with f in coefficient form, w in moment form\n   - Evaluates s(X) = sum_y f(X,y) * w(X,y) for X in {1,2}\n   - Algorithm:\n     * Pair up coefficients: (c0, c1), (m0, m1) at indices (2y, 2y+1)\n     * Compute: \n       - f_1 = c0 + c1,     w_1 = m1,       term_1 = f_1 * w_1\n       - f_2 = c0 + 2*c1,   w_2 = 3*m1 - m0, term_2 = f_2 * w_2\n     * Block reduce sums within shared memory\n     * Output: [S_DEG=2] elements per block\n   - Shared memory: num_warps * sizeof(FpExt) = num_warps * 16 bytes\n   - Two-phase: main kernel + final reduce kernel\n   - Launcher: whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_launch_params (line 242)\n\n### 3. whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments_kernel (lines 141-166)\n   - Grid/Block: kernel_launch_params(height >> 1)\n   - Operation: Fold both coefficient and moment vectors for one WHIR round\n   - Algorithm (for each y from 0 to height/2):\n     * Read: c0=f_coeffs[2y], c1=f_coeffs[2y+1]\n     *       m0=w_moments[2y], m1=w_moments[2y+1]\n     * Compute: f_folded[y] = c0 + alpha * c1\n     *          w_folded[y] = (1 - alpha) * m0 + (2*alpha - 1) * m1\n     * Write: f_folded_coeffs[y], w_folded_moments[y]\n   - No shared memory, straightforward element-wise operation\n\n### 4. w_moments_accumulate_kernel (lines 196-221)\n   - Grid/Block: kernel_launch_params(height, 256)\n   - Operation: Update WHIR moment vector by adding gamma-weighted query terms\n   - Algorithm (for each row in height):\n     * Compute exponent = row index\n     * Compute power from pows2: z0^exponent via bit manipulation\n     * For each query i: multiply z_i^exponent * gamma^(i+1)\n     * w_moments[row] += gamma * z0^exponent + sum of query terms\n   - No shared memory, power computation via bit-indexed powers\n\n## Launcher Parameters Computed\n\n### kernel_launch_params (in launcher.cuh)\n   - Default: 256 threads per block\n   - Grids determined to cover entire problem size\n   - Likely defined as: num_blocks = ceil(size / 256)\n\n### whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_launch_params (line 242)\n   - kernel_launch_params(height >> 1, 256) - special case for sumcheck\n   - Computes required temp buffer size = grid.x * S_DEG (line 248)\n   - This controls allocation size for d_sumcheck_tmp\n\nEOF\ncat /tmp/kernel_details.txt\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1612,"cache_read_input_tokens":61534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1612,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsFWvH1ZUbtcR8rKDCrN4x","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"7db714a2-38f8-40c5-a28c-3aedce30e33d"}
