tical I can actually implement: reducing the overhead in the GKR computation itself.\n\nI'm thinking about optimizing the Trace Commit phase by eliminating the separate bit-reversal pass and leveraging the NTT's native bit-reversal capability instead. Let me examine the NTT implementation to see if this is viable.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9701,"cache_read_input_tokens":184703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9701},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"8e2c53cc-f2c5-4d44-842e-e95ee90fb830"}
