{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CS9vZMDDo2NPbsgRRfJoFu","type":"tool_result","content":"135\t    return pow(x, static_cast<uint32_t>(n));\n136\t}\n137\t\n138\t/// Compute the multiplicative inverse of an FpExt.\n139\t__device__ inline FpExt inv(FpExt in) {\n140\t    FpExt result;\n141\t    result.rep = in.rep.reciprocal();\n142\t    return result;\n143\t}\n144\t\n145\t// TODO: find the difference between binomial_inversion and inv\n146\t__device__ __inline__ FpExt binomial_inversion(const FpExt &in) {\n147\t    constexpr uint32_t dth_root_u32 = 1728404513;\n148\t    constexpr uint32_t w = 11;\n149\t    Fp D(dth_root_u32);\n150\t    Fp W(w);\n151\t\n152\t    FpExt f(1);\n153\t    Fp D2 = D * D;\n154\t    Fp D3 = D2 * D;\n155\t    for (int i = 1; i < 4; ++i) {\n156\t        f = f * in;\n157\t        f.elems[1] *= D;\n158\t        f.elems[2] *= D2;\n159\t        f.elems[3] *= D3;\n160\t    }\n161\t    Fp g = (in.elems[1] * f.elems[3] + in.elems[2] * f.elems[2] + in.elems[3] * f.elems[1]) * W +\n162\t           in.elems[0] * f.elems[0];\n163\t    return f * FpExt(inv(g));\n164\t}\n165\t\n166\tstatic_assert(sizeof(FpExt) == 16, \"FpExt must be 16 bytes\");\n167\tstatic_assert(sizeof(FpExt) == sizeof(bb31_4_t), \"FpExt and bb31_4_t sizes must match\");\n168\tstatic_assert(alignof(FpExt) == alignof(bb31_4_t), \"FpExt and bb31_4_t align must match\");"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"b4775bb7-adc2-4f2a-9743-d5385aa6acc7","timestamp":"2026-04-16T03:51:52.092Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h","content":"    return pow(x, static_cast<uint32_t>(n));\n}\n\n/// Compute the multiplicative inverse of an FpExt.\n__device__ inline FpExt inv(FpExt in) {\n    FpExt result;\n    result.rep = in.rep.reciprocal();\n    return result;\n}\n\n// TODO: find the difference between binomial_inversion and inv\n__device__ __inline__ FpExt binomial_inversion(const FpExt &in) {\n    constexpr uint32_t dth_root_u32 = 1728404513;\n    constexpr uint32_t w = 11;\n    Fp D(dth_root_u32);\n    Fp W(w);\n\n    FpExt f(1);\n    Fp D2 = D * D;\n    Fp D3 = D2 * D;\n    for (int i = 1; i < 4; ++i) {\n        f = f * in;\n        f.elems[1] *= D;\n        f.elems[2] *= D2;\n        f.elems[3] *= D3;\n    }\n    Fp g = (in.elems[1] * f.elems[3] + in.elems[2] * f.elems[2] + in.elems[3] * f.elems[1]) * W +\n           in.elems[0] * f.elems[0];\n    return f * FpExt(inv(g));\n}\n\nstatic_assert(sizeof(FpExt) == 16, \"FpExt must be 16 bytes\");\nstatic_assert(sizeof(FpExt) == sizeof(bb31_4_t), \"FpExt and bb31_4_t sizes must match\");\nstatic_assert(alignof(FpExt) == alignof(bb31_4_t), \"FpExt and bb31_4_t align must match\");","numLines":34,"startLine":135,"totalLines":168}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019iLihasx5xLaDFKGvXuHhi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the `inv(FpExt)` function: it delegates to `bb31_4_t::reciprocal()` from the sppark library. The `reciprocal()` function likely uses the tower-based inversion for the degree-4 extension field.\n\nLooking at `baby_bear.hpp:571-578`, the inversion involves:\n```cpp\nbb31_t inv = b0*b0 - beta*b2*b2;\ninv = 1/inv;\nb0 *= inv;\n\n\nb2 *= inv;\n```\n\nThis is a tower-based inversion: first compute the norm in the quadratic subfield (b0² - β·b2²), then invert that norm (a single Fp inversion), then scale both components. The Fp inversion uses Fermat's little theorem (x^{p-2}), which for BabyBear (p = 2^31 - 1) costs roughly 30 squarings and 10 multiplications, making the total FpExt inversion about 2 multiplications and 1 subtraction for the norm, plus those 30 squarings and 10 multiplications for the field inversion.\n\nNow looking at the `compute_round_and_revert_kernel`, each element goes through 2 calls to `frac_unadd_inplace` (one for even, one for odd), and each call involves 1 FpExt inversion plus 3 FpExt multiplications. That works out to roughly 112 Fp multiplications per element just for the revert operation, while the actual computation takes about 80 Fp multiplications. So the revert is consuming around 58% of the total cost—still dominant, though not as extreme as my initial 90% estimate. Eliminating the revert would provide meaningful savings.\n\nIf I can skip the revert step, that's roughly 17-23ms saved from the kernel's 70ms runtime, potentially another 20-30ms from avoiding the initial tree revert steps. The approach is feasible: I'd keep a backup copy of the tree buffer before building, then use the non-revert variant for the first GKR round instead of the standard sumcheck-and-revert. It requires some memory overhead for the leaf backup and changes to the round orchestration, but the implementation is straightforward since the non-revert kernel is already available.\n\nNow I'm checking whether the revert is actually a necessary side effect for downstream operations. After the revert happens, the layer buffer contains un-combined values, and those need to be folded for the next round using either the PrecomputeM strategy or the FoldEval strategy. I need to verify whether skipping the revert would break this folding step.\n\nIf I use `compute_round_and_fold` instead, the fold is already integrated into the computation and the output is ready for the next round—which is what FoldEval does. But PrecomputeM needs those un-combined values for M matrix precomputation across multiple rounds, so it reads from the reverted buffer. I could modify the PrecomputeM path to read from the backup buffer instead of relying on the in-place revert, which means passing the backup buffer to the precompute_m function rather than the reverted one. This should be feasible.\n\nNow I need to look at the fractional.rs code to understand how the GKR round strategy selection works and where `compute_round_and_revert` is actually being called.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":231595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"f87aa7ae-167a-4240-ab4f-c13a83a8db0a"}
