f_backup = layer.clone_device(); // D2D copy\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::clone_device()` may need to be added if not present — it should allocate a new buffer and `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2D)`. Check if the existing `clone()` or a manual allocation + `cuda_memcpy` is needed.\n\n### Change 2: Add a new CUDA kernel `compute_round_from_leaves_kernel`\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: Add a kernel that reads from a SEPARATE read-only source buffer (the backup) instead of reverting the tree buffer in-place. The kernel:\n- Reads `(p0_even, q0_even) = src[idx]` and `(p1_even, q1_even) = src[idx + half]` directly (NO `inv()`)\n- Reads `(p0_odd, q0_odd) = src[idx + quarter]` and `(p1_odd, q1_odd) = src[idx + half + quarter]`\n- Computes polynomial contributions via `accumulate_compute_contributions` (identical to existing kernel)\n- Outputs block sums (identical to existing kernel)\n- Does NOT write to any tree buffer\n\nThis is essentially `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` with the revert logic (lines 466-486) replaced by direct reads, and no writes to the tree buffer.\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void compute_round_from_leaves_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n    const FracExt *__restrict__ src,  // Read-only source (leaf backup)\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n    FpExt lambda,\n    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n) {\n    // Same grid/block/shared as compute_round_and_revert_kernel\n    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n\n    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n    uint32_t idx_base = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n\n    for (uint32_t idx = idx_base; idx < num_x / 2; idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        // Direct reads from backup — NO field inversion\n        auto [p0_even, q0_even] = src[idx];\n        auto [p1_even, q1_even] = src[idx + half];\n        auto [p0_odd, q0_odd] = src[idx + quarter];\n        auto [p1_odd, q1_odd] = src[idx + half + quarter];\n\n        // Polynomial computation (identical to existing kernel)\n        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n            local0, local1\n        );\n    }\n\n    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n}\n```\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI binding and Rust wrapper\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n**What**: Add `extern \"C\"` declaration for `_frac_compute_round_from_leaves` and a safe Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_leaves(eq_buffer, src, num_x, lambda, d_sum_evals, tmp_block_sums)`.\n\n### Change 4: Add launcher in gkr.cu\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: Add `extern \"C\" int _frac_compute_round_from_leaves(...)` launcher function with same grid/block calculation as the existing `_frac_compute_round_and_revert`.\n\n### Change 5: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves` Rust function\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: New function parallel to `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert` but using `frac_compute_round_from_leaves` instead:\n```rust\nfn do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves<SC, TS>(\n    eq_buffer: &mut SqrtEqLayers,\n    leaf_backup: &DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    pq_size: usize,\n    lambda: EF,\n    transcript: &mut TS,\n    d_sum_evals: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    tmp_block_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    round_polys_eval: &mut Vec<[EF; GKR_S_DEG]>,\n    r_vec: &mut Vec<EF>,\n    prev_s_eval: &mut EF,\n    xi_j: EF,\n    eq_r_acc: &mut EF,\n) -> Result<EF, FractionalSumcheckError>\n```\n\n### Change 6: Replace last outer round's inner round 0 with leaf-based variant\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: The inner round 0 call at line 698\n**What**: For the LAST outer round only (when `round == total_rounds - 1`), replace `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, ...)` with `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(&leaf_backup, ...)`.\n\nAfter this, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`, since `layer` was not reverted:\n\n```rust\nif round == total_rounds - 1 {\n    // Last outer round: use backup instead of reverting\n    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &leaf_backup, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r0;\n    // First fused round reads from leaf_backup instead of layer\n    // Use BufferScheduler but with initial source = leaf_backup\n    // ... (see below)\n} else {\n    // Other outer rounds: use existing revert path\n    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r0;\n}\n```\n\nFor the last outer round's fused rounds, the FIRST fused round source must be `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`. The `BufferScheduler`'s first target should be `BackupToWork` (read from leaf_backup, fold to work_buffer). Subsequent fused rounds operate normally (work ↔ layer ping-pong).\n\n### Change 7: Adjust BufferScheduler for leaf-backup source\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: Add a `BackupToWork` variant to `BufferTarget` or handle the first fused round's source specially when the backup path is used. The simplest approach:\n\n```rust\n// For last outer round, first fused inner round:\nlet r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n    &mut eq_buffer,\n    &leaf_backup,  // source: backup instead of layer\n    &mut work_buffer,\n    pq_size,  // src_pq_size (before fold)\n    lambda, prev_r, transcript,\n    &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n    &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval,\n    xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n)?;\nprev_r = r1;\npq_size >>= 1;\n// Subsequent fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\nlet mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\nscheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;  // Override: data is in work_buffer, not layer\n```\n\nThis requires making `data_in_work_buffer` field `pub(super)` or adding a constructor that starts with data in the work buffer.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The compute kernel must produce identical s'(1) and s'(2) values. The only change is HOW the (p0/q0, p1/q1) values are obtained — from backup reads vs. in-place revert — not WHAT values are used.\n2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round after the backup-based compute must fold from backup (which has the same values as the reverted layer would have) to work_buffer using r0. This produces the same folded output.\n3. **Buffer lifecycle**: `leaf_backup` must remain allocated until the last outer round completes. It can be freed after.\n4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged — still use `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert`.\n5. **PrecomputeM strategy**: For the last outer round, if `PrecomputeM` strategy is selected, the backup path must provide the same leaf values to `frac_precompute_m_build_raw` and `frac_multifold_raw`. This may require routing the backup buffer to the PrecomputeM code path. If complex, scope to `FoldEval` strategy only and fall back to revert for PrecomputeM at the last round (conservative approach).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n2. Compare `STARK excl trace` and `LogUp GKR` metrics\n3. Expected: LogUp GKR improves by 15-25ms at APC 300 (50% of revert kernel time for last outer round)\n4. Expected: No regression at APC 0 (similar benefit but ~5 segments, so total savings ~5ms/seg)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms\n- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
