{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XcYJpDMwMXUNL2DwEybGXS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SEtZ2erRmKNRFtXdoFNDcu","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-eliminate-gkr-revert-field-inversions/plan.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11065,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3UPJ3vWYHw3TBLcB4xTbi","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"3573d510-7e6c-4bc2-bd2c-7606020c9fd8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SEtZ2erRmKNRFtXdoFNDcu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate the expensive `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversions in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck. The kernel is called once per outer round (inner round 0) and reverts the fractional evaluation tree one level by computing `inv(rhs.q)` per element — a tower-based FpExt reciprocal costing ~44 Fp multiplications. The revert is necessary because the tree was built in-place, overwriting original leaf values.\n6\t\n7\tBy saving a backup of the leaf buffer before tree building (~4 MB D2D copy at APC 300), the last outer round's inner round 0 can read original leaf values directly from the backup without field inversions. The last outer round processes the most elements (~N/2 = 65K at APC 300) and accounts for ~50% of total revert time.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)\n12\t1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(layer, total_rounds, alpha)` — bit-reverses the input and builds the first 2 tree layers in one fused pass. Modifies `layer` in-place.\n13\t2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers(&mut layer, half_i1)` loop — builds remaining tree layers in pairs. Each call combines `layer[idx]` with `layer[idx|half]` via `frac_add_inplace`, overwriting `layer[idx]`.\n14\t3. `frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, 2, true, ...)` — builds root and immediately reverts it.\n15\t\n16\tAfter tree building, the buffer layout is (for N = total_leaves):\n17\t- `layer[0]`: root (combined from all levels)\n18\t- `layer[1]`: root sibling\n19\t- `layer[2..3]`: level-(total_rounds-2) combined values\n20\t- ...\n21\t- `layer[N/4..N/2]`: level-0 combined \"rhs\" values (preserved from second tree build)\n22\t- `layer[N/2..N]`: original leaf \"rhs\" values (never overwritten after bit-reversal + first tree build)\n23\t\n24\t### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)\n25\tFor each outer round `r`, inner round 0 calls `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, lambda, ...)`.\n26\t\n27\tThis dispatches to `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (`gkr.cu:437-487`) which, per element:\n28\t1. Reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined value) and `rhs = layer[idx + half]` (preserved rhs)\n29\t2. Computes `rhs_q_inv = inv(rhs.q)` — **the expensive field inversion** (~44 Fp muls)\n30\t3. Recovers original lhs: `q0 = lhs.q * rhs_q_inv; p0 = (lhs.p - q0 * rhs.p) * rhs_q_inv`\n31\t4. **Writes reverted value back**: `layer[idx] = {p0, q0}`\n32\t5. Repeats for (idx + quarter, idx + half + quarter) pair\n33\t6. Computes polynomial contributions from the recovered values via `accumulate_compute_contributions`\n34\t\n35\t### Fused rounds (`fractional.rs:718+`)\n36\tInner rounds 1+ use `do_fused_sumcheck_round(src, dst, src_pq_size, lambda, r_prev, ...)`, calling `compute_round_and_fold_kernel` which reads from `src` without reversions and folds into `dst`.\n37\t\n38\tThe first fused round's source is the in-place-reverted `layer` (for `FoldEval` strategy, line 726: `do_fused_sumcheck_round(&layer, &mut work_buffer, ...)`).\n39\t\n40\t## Changes\n41\t\n42\t### Change 1: Save leaf backup before tree building\n43\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n44\t**Location**: Before `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call (~line 525)\n45\t**What**: Clone the `layer` DeviceBuffer to a new `leaf_backup` buffer. This is a D2D copy of the entire leaf buffer (~4 MB at APC 300, ~0.004ms at GPU memory bandwidth).\n46\t\n47\t```rust\n48\t// Save pre-tree-build leaf values for revert-free computation in last outer round\n49\tlet leaf_backup = layer.clone_device(); // D2D copy\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\tNote: `DeviceBuffer::clone_device()` may need to be added if not present — it should allocate a new buffer and `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2D)`. Check if the existing `clone()` or a manual allocation + `cuda_memcpy` is needed.\n53\t\n54\t### Change 2: Add a new CUDA kernel `compute_round_from_leaves_kernel`\n55\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n56\t**What**: Add a kernel that reads from a SEPARATE read-only source buffer (the backup) instead of reverting the tree buffer in-place. The kernel:\n57\t- Reads `(p0_even, q0_even) = src[idx]` and `(p1_even, q1_even) = src[idx + half]` directly (NO `inv()`)\n58\t- Reads `(p0_odd, q0_odd) = src[idx + quarter]` and `(p1_odd, q1_odd) = src[idx + half + quarter]`\n59\t- Computes polynomial contributions via `accumulate_compute_contributions` (identical to existing kernel)\n60\t- Outputs block sums (identical to existing kernel)\n61\t- Does NOT write to any tree buffer\n62\t\n63\tThis is essentially `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` with the revert logic (lines 466-486) replaced by direct reads, and no writes to the tree buffer.\n64\t\n65\t```cuda\n66\t__global__ void compute_round_from_leaves_kernel(\n67\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n68\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n69\t    const FracExt *__restrict__ src,  // Read-only source (leaf backup)\n70\t    uint32_t num_x,\n71\t    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n72\t    FpExt lambda,\n73\t    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n74\t) {\n75\t    // Same grid/block/shared as compute_round_and_revert_kernel\n76\t    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n77\t    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n78\t    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n79\t\n80\t    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n81\t    uint32_t idx_base = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n82\t\n83\t    for (uint32_t idx = idx_base; idx < num_x / 2; idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n84\t        // Direct reads from backup — NO field inversion\n85\t        auto [p0_even, q0_even] = src[idx];\n86\t        auto [p1_even, q1_even] = src[idx + half];\n87\t        auto [p0_odd, q0_odd] = src[idx + quarter];\n88\t        auto [p1_odd, q1_odd] = src[idx + half + quarter];\n89\t\n90\t        // Polynomial computation (identical to existing kernel)\n91\t        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n92\t            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n93\t            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n94\t            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n95\t            local0, local1\n96\t        );\n97\t    }\n98\t\n99\t    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n100\t}\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\t### Change 3: Add FFI binding and Rust wrapper\n104\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n105\t**What**: Add `extern \"C\"` declaration for `_frac_compute_round_from_leaves` and a safe Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_leaves(eq_buffer, src, num_x, lambda, d_sum_evals, tmp_block_sums)`.\n106\t\n107\t### Change 4: Add launcher in gkr.cu\n108\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n109\t**What**: Add `extern \"C\" int _frac_compute_round_from_leaves(...)` launcher function with same grid/block calculation as the existing `_frac_compute_round_and_revert`.\n110\t\n111\t### Change 5: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves` Rust function\n112\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n113\t**What**: New function parallel to `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert` but using `frac_compute_round_from_leaves` instead:\n114\t```rust\n115\tfn do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves<SC, TS>(\n116\t    eq_buffer: &mut SqrtEqLayers,\n117\t    leaf_backup: &DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n118\t    pq_size: usize,\n119\t    lambda: EF,\n120\t    transcript: &mut TS,\n121\t    d_sum_evals: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n122\t    tmp_block_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n123\t    round_polys_eval: &mut Vec<[EF; GKR_S_DEG]>,\n124\t    r_vec: &mut Vec<EF>,\n125\t    prev_s_eval: &mut EF,\n126\t    xi_j: EF,\n127\t    eq_r_acc: &mut EF,\n128\t) -> Result<EF, FractionalSumcheckError>\n129\t```\n130\t\n131\t### Change 6: Replace last outer round's inner round 0 with leaf-based variant\n132\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n133\t**Location**: The inner round 0 call at line 698\n134\t**What**: For the LAST outer round only (when `round == total_rounds - 1`), replace `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, ...)` with `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(&leaf_backup, ...)`.\n135\t\n136\tAfter this, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`, since `layer` was not reverted:\n137\t\n138\t```rust\n139\tif round == total_rounds - 1 {\n140\t    // Last outer round: use backup instead of reverting\n141\t    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(\n142\t        &mut eq_buffer, &leaf_backup, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n143\t        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n144\t        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n145\t    )?;\n146\t    prev_r = r0;\n147\t    // First fused round reads from leaf_backup instead of layer\n148\t    // Use BufferScheduler but with initial source = leaf_backup\n149\t    // ... (see below)\n150\t} else {\n151\t    // Other outer rounds: use existing revert path\n152\t    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n153\t        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n154\t        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n155\t        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n156\t    )?;\n157\t    prev_r = r0;\n158\t}\n159\t```\n160\t\n161\tFor the last outer round's fused rounds, the FIRST fused round source must be `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`. The `BufferScheduler`'s first target should be `BackupToWork` (read from leaf_backup, fold to work_buffer). Subsequent fused rounds operate normally (work ↔ layer ping-pong).\n162\t\n163\t### Change 7: Adjust BufferScheduler for leaf-backup source\n164\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n165\t**What**: Add a `BackupToWork` variant to `BufferTarget` or handle the first fused round's source specially when the backup path is used. The simplest approach:\n166\t\n167\t```rust\n168\t// For last outer round, first fused inner round:\n169\tlet r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n170\t    &mut eq_buffer,\n171\t    &leaf_backup,  // source: backup instead of layer\n172\t    &mut work_buffer,\n173\t    pq_size,  // src_pq_size (before fold)\n174\t    lambda, prev_r, transcript,\n175\t    &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n176\t    &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval,\n177\t    xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n178\t)?;\n179\tprev_r = r1;\n180\tpq_size >>= 1;\n181\t// Subsequent fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\n182\tlet mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\n183\tscheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;  // Override: data is in work_buffer, not layer\n184\t```\n185\t\n186\tThis requires making `data_in_work_buffer` field `pub(super)` or adding a constructor that starts with data in the work buffer.\n187\t\n188\t## Invariants\n189\t\n190\t1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The compute kernel must produce identical s'(1) and s'(2) values. The only change is HOW the (p0/q0, p1/q1) values are obtained — from backup reads vs. in-place revert — not WHAT values are used.\n191\t2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round after the backup-based compute must fold from backup (which has the same values as the reverted layer would have) to work_buffer using r0. This produces the same folded output.\n192\t3. **Buffer lifecycle**: `leaf_backup` must remain allocated until the last outer round completes. It can be freed after.\n193\t4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged — still use `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert`.\n194\t5. **PrecomputeM strategy**: For the last outer round, if `PrecomputeM` strategy is selected, the backup path must provide the same leaf values to `frac_precompute_m_build_raw` and `frac_multifold_raw`. This may require routing the backup buffer to the PrecomputeM code path. If complex, scope to `FoldEval` strategy only and fall back to revert for PrecomputeM at the last round (conservative approach).\n195\t\n196\t## Measurement Plan\n197\t\n198\t1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n199\t2. Compare `STARK excl trace` and `LogUp GKR` metrics\n200\t3. Expected: LogUp GKR improves by 15-25ms at APC 300 (50% of revert kernel time for last outer round)\n201\t4. Expected: No regression at APC 0 (similar benefit but ~5 segments, so total savings ~5ms/seg)\n202\t\n203\t## Rollback Criteria\n204\t\n205\t- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms\n206\t- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n207\t- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n208\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3UPJ3vWYHw3TBLcB4xTbi","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"16be9f43-5a5b-4f87-884a-0a3f07bd4d88","timestamp":"2026-04-16T03:59:50.236Z"}
