{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SVcyeCN4VUb15fazJHcKps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q1BU9dbYqASVqmgVix1Zw8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-eliminate-gkr-revert-field-inversions/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions (v2)\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversion writes in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck's last outer round by providing a pre-tree-build backup of leaf values. The revert currently writes recovered (un-combined) values back to the tree buffer (64 bytes per element); by reading originals from a backup instead, we eliminate both the `inv()` compute and the write-back traffic. At APC 300, the last outer round processes ~N/2 elements (the largest instance), and the write-back bandwidth dominates small-to-medium tree sizes.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)\n1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(buf, total_rounds, alpha)` — atomically fuses: (a) bit-reversal permutation, (b) alpha addition to ALL denominators (`q += alpha`), (c) tree layers 0+1 build via `frac_add_inplace`. Modifies buffer in-place.\n2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers` loop — builds remaining layers in pairs.\n3. `frac_build_tree_layer` — optional single remaining layer.\n4. Root extraction + revert (line 581).\n\n### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)\nFor each outer round `r`:\n- `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, ...)` calls `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (gkr.cu:437)\n- The kernel reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined) and `rhs = layer[idx+half]` (preserved)\n- Computes `inv(rhs.q)`, recovers original lhs, WRITES reverted value back to `layer[idx]`\n- Computes polynomial contributions from recovered values\n\n### Key problem with v1\nThe v1 plan proposed saving a backup BEFORE `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2`. This is wrong because the kernel fuses bit-reversal + alpha addition + 2 tree layers atomically. A pre-kernel backup has natural-order, no-alpha values — not the bit-reversed, alpha-applied leaves the revert recovers.\n\n## Changes (v2)\n\n### Change 1: Split the fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` for the large-N path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: Lines 525-532 (the `if total_leaves > 1024` branch)\n**What**: Replace the single fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call with separate operations:\n\n```rust\nlet start_layer_i = if total_leaves > 1024 {\n    // Step 1: Bit-reverse permutation\n    unsafe {\n        let buf = transmute::<&DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &DeviceBuffer<(EF, EF)>>(&layer);\n        bit_rev_frac_ext(buf, buf, total_rounds as u32, total_leaves as u32, 1)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::BitReversal)?;\n    }\n    // Step 2: Add alpha to all denominators\n    unsafe {\n        frac_add_alpha_all(&layer, alpha)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n    }\n    // Step 3: Save backup of post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree-build leaves\n    let leaf_backup = layer.clone_to_new_buffer()?;\n    // Step 4: Build tree layers 0+1\n    unsafe {\n        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves >> 1, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n    }\n    2\n} else {\n    // Small-N path unchanged — also save backup here\n    // ... (add backup after bitrev + alpha, before tree build)\n};\n```\n\n**New kernel needed**: `frac_add_alpha_all` — adds `alpha` to the `.q` field of ALL FracExt elements (not just the second half as the existing `frac_add_alpha` does). This is a simple element-wise kernel.\n\n**Performance impact of splitting**: The fused kernel saved ~1.5N global memory reads. Splitting adds ~1.5N reads back. For N = 2^21 = 2M elements: 2M × 32 bytes × 1.5 = 96 MB extra reads per call, at 1000 GB/s = 0.096ms per call. With ~6 calls: 0.58ms total overhead. Negligible vs expected savings.\n\n### Change 2: Add `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: A read-only variant of `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` that reads from a separate backup buffer:\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void compute_round_from_backup_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n    const FracExt *__restrict__ backup,  // Read-only: post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree leaves\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n    FpExt lambda,\n    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n) {\n    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n\n    for (uint32_t idx = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n         idx < num_x / 2;\n         idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x)\n    {\n        // Direct reads from backup — NO inv(), NO writes\n        FpExt p0_even = backup[idx].p,       q0_even = backup[idx].q;\n        FpExt p1_even = backup[idx+half].p,   q1_even = backup[idx+half].q;\n        FpExt p0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].p, q0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].q;\n        FpExt p1_odd  = backup[idx+half+quarter].p, q1_odd = backup[idx+half+quarter].q;\n\n        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n            local0, local1\n        );\n    }\n    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n}\n```\n\n**Key differences from `compute_round_and_revert_kernel`**:\n- Reads from `backup` (const), not `layer` (mutable)\n- No `inv(rhs.q)` call — reads original values directly\n- No writes to tree buffer — eliminates 64 bytes/element write traffic\n- Read traffic reduced from 128 bytes (4 FracExt from tree) to 128 bytes (4 FracExt from backup) — same read volume but no writes\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI bindings and launcher\n\n**Files**: `gkr.cu` (launcher), `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (FFI binding)\n**What**: Launcher `_frac_compute_round_from_backup(eq_low, eq_high, backup, num_x, eq_low_cap, lambda, out, tmp_block_sums)` and Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_backup(...)`.\n\n### Change 4: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_backup` Rust function\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: New function that calls `frac_compute_round_from_backup` instead of `frac_compute_round_and_revert`, then delegates to `observe_and_update` (same as existing).\n\n### Change 5: Use backup path for the last outer round\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: Inner round 0 dispatch (~line 698)\n**What**: When `round == total_rounds - 1` (last outer round):\n\n```rust\nlet r0 = if round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n    do_sumcheck_round_from_backup(\n        &mut eq_buffer, leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap(), pq_size, lambda,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?\n} else {\n    do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?\n};\n```\n\n### Change 6: Route first fused round to read from backup\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: For the last outer round, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`:\n\n```rust\n// For last outer round: first fused round reads from backup\nif round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n    let backup = leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap();\n    let r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n        &mut eq_buffer, backup, &mut work_buffer, pq_size, lambda, prev_r,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r1;\n    pq_size >>= 1;\n\n    // Remaining fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\n    let mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\n    scheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;\n    for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(2) {\n        // ... normal fused rounds with scheduler\n    }\n} else {\n    // ... existing non-backup path\n}\n```\n\n### Change 7: Handle PrecomputeM strategy\n\nFor the last outer round with `PrecomputeM` strategy, fall back to the existing revert path. This is the conservative approach:\n\n```rust\nlet use_backup = round == total_rounds - 1\n    && leaf_backup.is_some()\n    && matches!(backend, GkrRoundStrategy::FoldEval);\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The backup buffer contains exactly the pre-tree-build, post-bitrev, post-alpha leaf values. At the last outer round, these are the values that `compute_round_and_revert` would recover via `frac_unadd`. Reading them directly produces identical `(p0_even, q0_even, p1_even, q1_even, p0_odd, q0_odd, p1_odd, q1_odd)` values.\n2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round reads from `leaf_backup` (same data as the reverted layer would contain) and folds with `r0`. Subsequent rounds fold from work_buffer/layer normally.\n3. **Alpha application**: The backup has alpha already applied to all denominators (from the explicit `frac_add_alpha_all` step). This matches the post-bitrev-pre-tree state.\n4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged.\n5. **PrecomputeM fallback**: Last outer round with PrecomputeM uses the existing revert path.\n6. **Memory**: The backup buffer uses N FracExt elements of extra GPU memory. At APC 300 with N ≈ 2M: ~64 MB. Within budget.\n7. **Small-N fallback**: For total_leaves ≤ 1024, the code already uses separate bitrev + tree build. The backup can be inserted similarly.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n2. Compare `LogUp GKR`, `STARK excl trace` metrics\n3. Use nsight to verify `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instance count decreases (replaced by `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` for last outer round)\n4. Expected: ~5-15ms improvement on STARK excl trace at APC 300 (from eliminating revert writes and inv() compute for the largest tree level)\n5. Expected: No regression at APC 0\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 5ms\n- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":263137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3157},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"1b0c6879-31ec-4ffa-b43a-a30269b6dd84"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1BU9dbYqASVqmgVix1Zw8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-eliminate-gkr-revert-field-inversions/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"f9664c66-d2e5-40b7-8c89-1c06bad9195b","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:12:30.390Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-eliminate-gkr-revert-field-inversions/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions (v2)\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversion writes in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck's last outer round by providing a pre-tree-build backup of leaf values. The revert currently writes recovered (un-combined) values back to the tree buffer (64 bytes per element); by reading originals from a backup instead, we eliminate both the `inv()` compute and the write-back traffic. At APC 300, the last outer round processes ~N/2 elements (the largest instance), and the write-back bandwidth dominates small-to-medium tree sizes.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)\n1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(buf, total_rounds, alpha)` — atomically fuses: (a) bit-reversal permutation, (b) alpha addition to ALL denominators (`q += alpha`), (c) tree layers 0+1 build via `frac_add_inplace`. Modifies buffer in-place.\n2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers` loop — builds remaining layers in pairs.\n3. `frac_build_tree_layer` — optional single remaining layer.\n4. Root extraction + revert (line 581).\n\n### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)\nFor each outer round `r`:\n- `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, ...)` calls `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (gkr.cu:437)\n- The kernel reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined) and `rhs = layer[idx+half]` (preserved)\n- Computes `inv(rhs.q)`, recovers original lhs, WRITES reverted value back to `layer[idx]`\n- Computes polynomial contributions from recovered values\n\n### Key problem with v1\nThe v1 plan proposed saving a backup BEFORE `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2`. This is wrong because the kernel fuses bit-reversal + alpha addition + 2 tree layers atomically. A pre-kernel backup has natural-order, no-alpha values — not the bit-reversed, alpha-applied leaves the revert recovers.\n\n## Changes (v2)\n\n### Change 1: Split the fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` for the large-N path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: Lines 525-532 (the `if total_leaves > 1024` branch)\n**What**: Replace the single fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call with separate operations:\n\n```rust\nlet start_layer_i = if total_leaves > 1024 {\n    // Step 1: Bit-reverse permutation\n    unsafe {\n        let buf = transmute::<&DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &DeviceBuffer<(EF, EF)>>(&layer);\n        bit_rev_frac_ext(buf, buf, total_rounds as u32, total_leaves as u32, 1)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::BitReversal)?;\n    }\n    // Step 2: Add alpha to all denominators\n    unsafe {\n        frac_add_alpha_all(&layer, alpha)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n    }\n    // Step 3: Save backup of post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree-build leaves\n    let leaf_backup = layer.clone_to_new_buffer()?;\n    // Step 4: Build tree layers 0+1\n    unsafe {\n        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves >> 1, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n    }\n    2\n} else {\n    // Small-N path unchanged — also save backup here\n    // ... (add backup after bitrev + alpha, before tree build)\n};\n```\n\n**New kernel needed**: `frac_add_alpha_all` — adds `alpha` to the `.q` field of ALL FracExt elements (not just the second half as the existing `frac_add_alpha` does). This is a simple element-wise kernel.\n\n**Performance impact of splitting**: The fused kernel saved ~1.5N global memory reads. Splitting adds ~1.5N reads back. For N = 2^21 = 2M elements: 2M × 32 bytes × 1.5 = 96 MB extra reads per call, at 1000 GB/s = 0.096ms per call. With ~6 calls: 0.58ms total overhead. Negligible vs expected savings.\n\n### Change 2: Add `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: A read-only variant of `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` that reads from a separate backup buffer:\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void compute_round_from_backup_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n    const FracExt *__restrict__ backup,  // Read-only: post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree leaves\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n    FpExt lambda,\n    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n) {\n    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n\n    for (uint32_t idx = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n         idx < num_x / 2;\n         idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x)\n    {\n        // Direct reads from backup — NO inv(), NO writes\n        FpExt p0_even = backup[idx].p,       q0_even = backup[idx].q;\n        FpExt p1_even = backup[idx+half].p,   q1_even = backup[idx+half].q;\n        FpExt p0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].p, q0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].q;\n        FpExt p1_odd  = backup[idx+half+quarter].p, q1_odd = backup[idx+half+quarter].q;\n\n        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n            local0, local1\n        );\n    }\n    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n}\n```\n\n**Key differences from `compute_round_and_revert_kernel`**:\n- Reads from `backup` (const), not `layer` (mutable)\n- No `inv(rhs.q)` call — reads original values directly\n- No writes to tree buffer — eliminates 64 bytes/element write traffic\n- Read traffic reduced from 128 bytes (4 FracExt from tree) to 128 bytes (4 FracExt from backup) — same read volume but no writes\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI bindings and launcher\n\n**Files**: `gkr.cu` (launcher), `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (FFI binding)\n**What**: Launcher `_frac_compute_round_from_backup(eq_low, eq_high, backup, num_x, eq_low_cap, lambda, out, tmp_block_sums)` and Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_backup(...)`.\n\n### Change 4: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_backup` Rust function\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: New function that calls `frac_compute_round_from_backup` instead of `frac_compute_round_and_revert`, then delegates to `observe_and_update` (same as existing).\n\n### Change 5: Use backup path for the last outer round\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: Inner round 0 dispatch (~line 698)\n**What**: When `round == total_rounds - 1` (last outer round):\n\n```rust\nlet r0 = if round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n    do_sumcheck_round_from_backup(\n        &mut eq_buffer, leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap(), pq_size, lambda,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?\n} else {\n    do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?\n};\n```\n\n### Change 6: Route first fused round to read from backup\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: For the last outer round, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`:\n\n```rust\n// For last outer round: first fused round reads from backup\nif round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n    let backup = leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap();\n    let r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n        &mut eq_buffer, backup, &mut work_buffer, pq_size, lambda, prev_r,\n        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r1;\n    pq_size >>= 1;\n\n    // Remaining fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\n    let mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\n    scheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;\n    for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(2) {\n        // ... normal fused rounds with scheduler\n    }\n} else {\n    // ... existing non-backup path\n}\n```\n\n### Change 7: Handle PrecomputeM strategy\n\nFor the last outer round with `PrecomputeM` strategy, fall back to the existing revert path. This is the conservative approach:\n\n```rust\nlet use_backup = round == total_rounds - 1\n    && leaf_backup.is_some()\n    && matches!(backend, GkrRoundStrategy::FoldEval);\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The backup buffer contains exactly the pre-tree-build, post-bitrev, post-alpha leaf values. At the last outer round, these are the values that `compute_round_and_revert` would recover via `frac_unadd`. Reading them directly produces identical `(p0_even, q0_even, p1_even, q1_even, p0_odd, q0_odd, p1_odd, q1_odd)` values.\n2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round reads from `leaf_backup` (same data as the reverted layer would contain) and folds with `r0`. Subsequent rounds fold from work_buffer/layer normally.\n3. **Alpha application**: The backup has alpha already applied to all denominators (from the explicit `frac_add_alpha_all` step). This matches the post-bitrev-pre-tree state.\n4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged.\n5. **PrecomputeM fallback**: Last outer round with PrecomputeM uses the existing revert path.\n6. **Memory**: The backup buffer uses N FracExt elements of extra GPU memory. At APC 300 with N ≈ 2M: ~64 MB. Within budget.\n7. **Small-N fallback**: For total_leaves ≤ 1024, the code already uses separate bitrev + tree build. The backup can be inserted similarly.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n2. Compare `LogUp GKR`, `STARK excl trace` metrics\n3. Use nsight to verify `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instance count decreases (replaced by `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` for last outer round)\n4. Expected: ~5-15ms improvement on STARK excl trace at APC 300 (from eliminating revert writes and inv() compute for the largest tree level)\n5. Expected: No regression at APC 0\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 5ms\n- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":93,"newStart":1,"newLines":98,"lines":["-# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions","+# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions (v2)"," "," ## Goal"," ","-Eliminate the expensive `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversions in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck. The kernel is called once per outer round (inner round 0) and reverts the fractional evaluation tree one level by computing `inv(rhs.q)` per element — a tower-based FpExt reciprocal costing ~44 Fp multiplications. The revert is necessary because the tree was built in-place, overwriting original leaf values.","+Eliminate the `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversion writes in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck's last outer round by providing a pre-tree-build backup of leaf values. The revert currently writes recovered (un-combined) values back to the tree buffer (64 bytes per element); by reading originals from a backup instead, we eliminate both the `inv()` compute and the write-back traffic. At APC 300, the last outer round processes ~N/2 elements (the largest instance), and the write-back bandwidth dominates small-to-medium tree sizes."," ","-By saving a backup of the leaf buffer before tree building (~4 MB D2D copy at APC 300), the last outer round's inner round 0 can read original leaf values directly from the backup without field inversions. The last outer round processes the most elements (~N/2 = 65K at APC 300) and accounts for ~50% of total revert time.","-"," ## Current Code Path"," "," ### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)","-1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(layer, total_rounds, alpha)` — bit-reverses the input and builds the first 2 tree layers in one fused pass. Modifies `layer` in-place.","-2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers(&mut layer, half_i1)` loop — builds remaining tree layers in pairs. Each call combines `layer[idx]` with `layer[idx|half]` via `frac_add_inplace`, overwriting `layer[idx]`.","-3. `frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, 2, true, ...)` — builds root and immediately reverts it.","+1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(buf, total_rounds, alpha)` — atomically fuses: (a) bit-reversal permutation, (b) alpha addition to ALL denominators (`q += alpha`), (c) tree layers 0+1 build via `frac_add_inplace`. Modifies buffer in-place.","+2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers` loop — builds remaining layers in pairs.","+3. `frac_build_tree_layer` — optional single remaining layer.","+4. Root extraction + revert (line 581)."," ","-After tree building, the buffer layout is (for N = total_leaves):","-- `layer[0]`: root (combined from all levels)","-- `layer[1]`: root sibling","-- `layer[2..3]`: level-(total_rounds-2) combined values","-- ...","-- `layer[N/4..N/2]`: level-0 combined \"rhs\" values (preserved from second tree build)","-- `layer[N/2..N]`: original leaf \"rhs\" values (never overwritten after bit-reversal + first tree build)","-"," ### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)","-For each outer round `r`, inner round 0 calls `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, lambda, ...)`.","+For each outer round `r`:","+- `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, ...)` calls `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (gkr.cu:437)","+- The kernel reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined) and `rhs = layer[idx+half]` (preserved)","+- Computes `inv(rhs.q)`, recovers original lhs, WRITES reverted value back to `layer[idx]`","+- Computes polynomial contributions from recovered values"," ","-This dispatches to `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (`gkr.cu:437-487`) which, per element:","-1. Reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined value) and `rhs = layer[idx + half]` (preserved rhs)","-2. Computes `rhs_q_inv = inv(rhs.q)` — **the expensive field inversion** (~44 Fp muls)","-3. Recovers original lhs: `q0 = lhs.q * rhs_q_inv; p0 = (lhs.p - q0 * rhs.p) * rhs_q_inv`","-4. **Writes reverted value back**: `layer[idx] = {p0, q0}`","-5. Repeats for (idx + quarter, idx + half + quarter) pair","-6. Computes polynomial contributions from the recovered values via `accumulate_compute_contributions`","+### Key problem with v1","+The v1 plan proposed saving a backup BEFORE `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2`. This is wrong because the kernel fuses bit-reversal + alpha addition + 2 tree layers atomically. A pre-kernel backup has natural-order, no-alpha values — not the bit-reversed, alpha-applied leaves the revert recovers."," ","-### Fused rounds (`fractional.rs:718+`)","-Inner rounds 1+ use `do_fused_sumcheck_round(src, dst, src_pq_size, lambda, r_prev, ...)`, calling `compute_round_and_fold_kernel` which reads from `src` without reversions and folds into `dst`.","+## Changes (v2)"," ","-The first fused round's source is the in-place-reverted `layer` (for `FoldEval` strategy, line 726: `do_fused_sumcheck_round(&layer, &mut work_buffer, ...)`).","+### Change 1: Split the fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` for the large-N path"," ","-## Changes","-","-### Change 1: Save leaf backup before tree building"," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`","-**Location**: Before `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call (~line 525)","-**What**: Clone the `layer` DeviceBuffer to a new `leaf_backup` buffer. This is a D2D copy of the entire leaf buffer (~4 MB at APC 300, ~0.004ms at GPU memory bandwidth).","+**Location**: Lines 525-532 (the `if total_leaves > 1024` branch)","+**What**: Replace the single fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call with separate operations:"," "," ```rust","-// Save pre-tree-build leaf values for revert-free computation in last outer round","-let leaf_backup = layer.clone_device(); // D2D copy","+let start_layer_i = if total_leaves > 1024 {","+    // Step 1: Bit-reverse permutation","+    unsafe {","+        let buf = transmute::<&DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &DeviceBuffer<(EF, EF)>>(&layer);","+        bit_rev_frac_ext(buf, buf, total_rounds as u32, total_leaves as u32, 1)","+            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::BitReversal)?;","+    }","+    // Step 2: Add alpha to all denominators","+    unsafe {","+        frac_add_alpha_all(&layer, alpha)","+            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;","+    }","+    // Step 3: Save backup of post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree-build leaves","+    let leaf_backup = layer.clone_to_new_buffer()?;","+    // Step 4: Build tree layers 0+1","+    unsafe {","+        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves, false, EF::ZERO, false)","+            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;","+        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves >> 1, false, EF::ZERO, false)","+            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;","+    }","+    2","+} else {","+    // Small-N path unchanged — also save backup here","+    // ... (add backup after bitrev + alpha, before tree build)","+};"," ```"," ","-Note: `DeviceBuffer::clone_device()` may need to be added if not present — it should allocate a new buffer and `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2D)`. Check if the existing `clone()` or a manual allocation + `cuda_memcpy` is needed.","+**New kernel needed**: `frac_add_alpha_all` — adds `alpha` to the `.q` field of ALL FracExt elements (not just the second half as the existing `frac_add_alpha` does). This is a simple element-wise kernel."," ","-### Change 2: Add a new CUDA kernel `compute_round_from_leaves_kernel`","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`","-**What**: Add a kernel that reads from a SEPARATE read-only source buffer (the backup) instead of reverting the tree buffer in-place. The kernel:","-- Reads `(p0_even, q0_even) = src[idx]` and `(p1_even, q1_even) = src[idx + half]` directly (NO `inv()`)","-- Reads `(p0_odd, q0_odd) = src[idx + quarter]` and `(p1_odd, q1_odd) = src[idx + half + quarter]`","-- Computes polynomial contributions via `accumulate_compute_contributions` (identical to existing kernel)","-- Outputs block sums (identical to existing kernel)","-- Does NOT write to any tree buffer","+**Performance impact of splitting**: The fused kernel saved ~1.5N global memory reads. Splitting adds ~1.5N reads back. For N = 2^21 = 2M elements: 2M × 32 bytes × 1.5 = 96 MB extra reads per call, at 1000 GB/s = 0.096ms per call. With ~6 calls: 0.58ms total overhead. Negligible vs expected savings."," ","-This is essentially `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` with the revert logic (lines 466-486) replaced by direct reads, and no writes to the tree buffer.","+### Change 2: Add `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` CUDA kernel"," ","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`","+**What**: A read-only variant of `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` that reads from a separate backup buffer:","+"," ```cuda","-__global__ void compute_round_from_leaves_kernel(","+__global__ void compute_round_from_backup_kernel(","     const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,","     const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,","-    const FracExt *__restrict__ src,  // Read-only source (leaf backup)","+    const FracExt *__restrict__ backup,  // Read-only: post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree leaves","     uint32_t num_x,","     uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,","     FpExt lambda,","     FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums"," ) {","-    // Same grid/block/shared as compute_round_and_revert_kernel","     extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];","     const uint32_t half = num_x;","     const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;","-","     FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());","-    uint32_t idx_base = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;"," ","-    for (uint32_t idx = idx_base; idx < num_x / 2; idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {","-        // Direct reads from backup — NO field inversion","-        auto [p0_even, q0_even] = src[idx];","-        auto [p1_even, q1_even] = src[idx + half];","-        auto [p0_odd, q0_odd] = src[idx + quarter];","-        auto [p1_odd, q1_odd] = src[idx + half + quarter];","+    for (uint32_t idx = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;","+         idx < num_x / 2;","+         idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x)","+    {","+        // Direct reads from backup — NO inv(), NO writes","+        FpExt p0_even = backup[idx].p,       q0_even = backup[idx].q;","+        FpExt p1_even = backup[idx+half].p,   q1_even = backup[idx+half].q;","+        FpExt p0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].p, q0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].q;","+        FpExt p1_odd  = backup[idx+half+quarter].p, q1_odd = backup[idx+half+quarter].q;"," ","-        // Polynomial computation (identical to existing kernel)","         accumulate_compute_contributions(","             eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,","             p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,"]},{"oldStart":95,"oldLines":113,"newStart":100,"newLines":106,"lines":["             local0, local1","         );","     }","-","     reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);"," }"," ```"," ","-### Change 3: Add FFI binding and Rust wrapper","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`","-**What**: Add `extern \"C\"` declaration for `_frac_compute_round_from_leaves` and a safe Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_leaves(eq_buffer, src, num_x, lambda, d_sum_evals, tmp_block_sums)`.","+**Key differences from `compute_round_and_revert_kernel`**:","+- Reads from `backup` (const), not `layer` (mutable)","+- No `inv(rhs.q)` call — reads original values directly","+- No writes to tree buffer — eliminates 64 bytes/element write traffic","+- Read traffic reduced from 128 bytes (4 FracExt from tree) to 128 bytes (4 FracExt from backup) — same read volume but no writes"," ","-### Change 4: Add launcher in gkr.cu","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`","-**What**: Add `extern \"C\" int _frac_compute_round_from_leaves(...)` launcher function with same grid/block calculation as the existing `_frac_compute_round_and_revert`.","+### Change 3: Add FFI bindings and launcher"," ","-### Change 5: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves` Rust function","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`","-**What**: New function parallel to `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert` but using `frac_compute_round_from_leaves` instead:","-```rust","-fn do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves<SC, TS>(","-    eq_buffer: &mut SqrtEqLayers,","-    leaf_backup: &DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,","-    pq_size: usize,","-    lambda: EF,","-    transcript: &mut TS,","-    d_sum_evals: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,","-    tmp_block_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,","-    round_polys_eval: &mut Vec<[EF; GKR_S_DEG]>,","-    r_vec: &mut Vec<EF>,","-    prev_s_eval: &mut EF,","-    xi_j: EF,","-    eq_r_acc: &mut EF,","-) -> Result<EF, FractionalSumcheckError>","-```","+**Files**: `gkr.cu` (launcher), `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (FFI binding)","+**What**: Launcher `_frac_compute_round_from_backup(eq_low, eq_high, backup, num_x, eq_low_cap, lambda, out, tmp_block_sums)` and Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_backup(...)`."," ","-### Change 6: Replace last outer round's inner round 0 with leaf-based variant","+### Change 4: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_backup` Rust function","+"," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`","-**Location**: The inner round 0 call at line 698","-**What**: For the LAST outer round only (when `round == total_rounds - 1`), replace `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, ...)` with `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(&leaf_backup, ...)`.","+**What**: New function that calls `frac_compute_round_from_backup` instead of `frac_compute_round_and_revert`, then delegates to `observe_and_update` (same as existing)."," ","-After this, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`, since `layer` was not reverted:","+### Change 5: Use backup path for the last outer round"," ","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`","+**Location**: Inner round 0 dispatch (~line 698)","+**What**: When `round == total_rounds - 1` (last outer round):","+"," ```rust","-if round == total_rounds - 1 {","-    // Last outer round: use backup instead of reverting","-    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(","-        &mut eq_buffer, &leaf_backup, pq_size, lambda, transcript,","-        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","+let r0 = if round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {","+    do_sumcheck_round_from_backup(","+        &mut eq_buffer, leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap(), pq_size, lambda,","+        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","         &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,","-    )?;","-    prev_r = r0;","-    // First fused round reads from leaf_backup instead of layer","-    // Use BufferScheduler but with initial source = leaf_backup","-    // ... (see below)","+    )?"," } else {","-    // Other outer rounds: use existing revert path","-    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(","-        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda, transcript,","-        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","+    do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(","+        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda,","+        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","         &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,","-    )?;","-    prev_r = r0;","-}","+    )?","+};"," ```"," ","-For the last outer round's fused rounds, the FIRST fused round source must be `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`. The `BufferScheduler`'s first target should be `BackupToWork` (read from leaf_backup, fold to work_buffer). Subsequent fused rounds operate normally (work ↔ layer ping-pong).","+### Change 6: Route first fused round to read from backup"," ","-### Change 7: Adjust BufferScheduler for leaf-backup source"," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`","-**What**: Add a `BackupToWork` variant to `BufferTarget` or handle the first fused round's source specially when the backup path is used. The simplest approach:","+**What**: For the last outer round, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`:"," "," ```rust","-// For last outer round, first fused inner round:","-let r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(","-    &mut eq_buffer,","-    &leaf_backup,  // source: backup instead of layer","-    &mut work_buffer,","-    pq_size,  // src_pq_size (before fold)","-    lambda, prev_r, transcript,","-    &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","-    &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval,","-    xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,","-)?;","-prev_r = r1;","-pq_size >>= 1;","-// Subsequent fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer","-let mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);","-scheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;  // Override: data is in work_buffer, not layer","+// For last outer round: first fused round reads from backup","+if round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {","+    let backup = leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap();","+    let r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(","+        &mut eq_buffer, backup, &mut work_buffer, pq_size, lambda, prev_r,","+        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,","+        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,","+    )?;","+    prev_r = r1;","+    pq_size >>= 1;","+","+    // Remaining fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer","+    let mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);","+    scheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;","+    for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(2) {","+        // ... normal fused rounds with scheduler","+    }","+} else {","+    // ... existing non-backup path","+}"," ```"," ","-This requires making `data_in_work_buffer` field `pub(super)` or adding a constructor that starts with data in the work buffer.","+### Change 7: Handle PrecomputeM strategy"," ","+For the last outer round with `PrecomputeM` strategy, fall back to the existing revert path. This is the conservative approach:","+","+```rust","+let use_backup = round == total_rounds - 1","+    && leaf_backup.is_some()","+    && matches!(backend, GkrRoundStrategy::FoldEval);","+```","+"," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The compute kernel must produce identical s'(1) and s'(2) values. The only change is HOW the (p0/q0, p1/q1) values are obtained — from backup reads vs. in-place revert — not WHAT values are used.","-2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round after the backup-based compute must fold from backup (which has the same values as the reverted layer would have) to work_buffer using r0. This produces the same folded output.","-3. **Buffer lifecycle**: `leaf_backup` must remain allocated until the last outer round completes. It can be freed after.","-4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged — still use `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert`.","-5. **PrecomputeM strategy**: For the last outer round, if `PrecomputeM` strategy is selected, the backup path must provide the same leaf values to `frac_precompute_m_build_raw` and `frac_multifold_raw`. This may require routing the backup buffer to the PrecomputeM code path. If complex, scope to `FoldEval` strategy only and fall back to revert for PrecomputeM at the last round (conservative approach).","+1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The backup buffer contains exactly the pre-tree-build, post-bitrev, post-alpha leaf values. At the last outer round, these are the values that `compute_round_and_revert` would recover via `frac_unadd`. Reading them directly produces identical `(p0_even, q0_even, p1_even, q1_even, p0_odd, q0_odd, p1_odd, q1_odd)` values.","+2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round reads from `leaf_backup` (same data as the reverted layer would contain) and folds with `r0`. Subsequent rounds fold from work_buffer/layer normally.","+3. **Alpha application**: The backup has alpha already applied to all denominators (from the explicit `frac_add_alpha_all` step). This matches the post-bitrev-pre-tree state.","+4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged.","+5. **PrecomputeM fallback**: Last outer round with PrecomputeM uses the existing revert path.","+6. **Memory**: The backup buffer uses N FracExt elements of extra GPU memory. At APC 300 with N ≈ 2M: ~64 MB. Within budget.","+7. **Small-N fallback**: For total_leaves ≤ 1024, the code already uses separate bitrev + tree build. The backup can be inserted similarly."," "," ## Measurement Plan"," "," 1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300","-2. Compare `STARK excl trace` and `LogUp GKR` metrics","-3. Expected: LogUp GKR improves by 15-25ms at APC 300 (50% of revert kernel time for last outer round)","-4. Expected: No regression at APC 0 (similar benefit but ~5 segments, so total savings ~5ms/seg)","+2. Compare `LogUp GKR`, `STARK excl trace` metrics","+3. Use nsight to verify `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instance count decreases (replaced by `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` for last outer round)","+4. Expected: ~5-15ms improvement on STARK excl trace at APC 300 (from eliminating revert writes and inv() compute for the largest tree level)","+5. Expected: No regression at APC 0"," "," ## Rollback Criteria"," ","-- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms","+- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 5ms"," - Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms"," - Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the expensive `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversions in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck. The kernel is called once per outer round (inner round 0) and reverts the fractional evaluation tree one level by computing `inv(rhs.q)` per element — a tower-based FpExt reciprocal costing ~44 Fp multiplications. The revert is necessary because the tree was built in-place, overwriting original leaf values.\n\nBy saving a backup of the leaf buffer before tree building (~4 MB D2D copy at APC 300), the last outer round's inner round 0 can read original leaf values directly from the backup without field inversions. The last outer round processes the most elements (~N/2 = 65K at APC 300) and accounts for ~50% of total revert time.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)\n1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(layer, total_rounds, alpha)` — bit-reverses the input and builds the first 2 tree layers in one fused pass. Modifies `layer` in-place.\n2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers(&mut layer, half_i1)` loop — builds remaining tree layers in pairs. Each call combines `layer[idx]` with `layer[idx|half]` via `frac_add_inplace`, overwriting `layer[idx]`.\n3. `frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, 2, true, ...)` — builds root and immediately reverts it.\n\nAfter tree building, the buffer layout is (for N = total_leaves):\n- `layer[0]`: root (combined from all levels)\n- `layer[1]`: root sibling\n- `layer[2..3]`: level-(total_rounds-2) combined values\n- ...\n- `layer[N/4..N/2]`: level-0 combined \"rhs\" values (preserved from second tree build)\n- `layer[N/2..N]`: original leaf \"rhs\" values (never overwritten after bit-reversal + first tree build)\n\n### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)\nFor each outer round `r`, inner round 0 calls `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, lambda, ...)`.\n\nThis dispatches to `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (`gkr.cu:437-487`) which, per element:\n1. Reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined value) and `rhs = layer[idx + half]` (preserved rhs)\n2. Computes `rhs_q_inv = inv(rhs.q)` — **the expensive field inversion** (~44 Fp muls)\n3. Recovers original lhs: `q0 = lhs.q * rhs_q_inv; p0 = (lhs.p - q0 * rhs.p) * rhs_q_inv`\n4. **Writes reverted value back**: `layer[idx] = {p0, q0}`\n5. Repeats for (idx + quarter, idx + half + quarter) pair\n6. Computes polynomial contributions from the recovered values via `accumulate_compute_contributions`\n\n### Fused rounds (`fractional.rs:718+`)\nInner rounds 1+ use `do_fused_sumcheck_round(src, dst, src_pq_size, lambda, r_prev, ...)`, calling `compute_round_and_fold_kernel` which reads from `src` without reversions and folds into `dst`.\n\nThe first fused round's source is the in-place-reverted `layer` (for `FoldEval` strategy, line 726: `do_fused_sumcheck_round(&layer, &mut work_buffer, ...)`).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Save leaf backup before tree building\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: Before `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call (~line 525)\n**What**: Clone the `layer` DeviceBuffer to a new `leaf_backup` buffer. This is a D2D copy of the entire leaf buffer (~4 MB at APC 300, ~0.004ms at GPU memory bandwidth).\n\n```rust\n// Save pre-tree-build leaf values for revert-free computation in last outer round\nlet leaf_backup = layer.clone_device(); // D2D copy\n```\n\nNote: `DeviceBuffer::clone_device()` may need to be added if not present — it should allocate a new buffer and `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2D)`. Check if the existing `clone()` or a manual allocation + `cuda_memcpy` is needed.\n\n### Change 2: Add a new CUDA kernel `compute_round_from_leaves_kernel`\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: Add a kernel that reads from a SEPARATE read-only source buffer (the backup) instead of reverting the tree buffer in-place. The kernel:\n- Reads `(p0_even, q0_even) = src[idx]` and `(p1_even, q1_even) = src[idx + half]` directly (NO `inv()`)\n- Reads `(p0_odd, q0_odd) = src[idx + quarter]` and `(p1_odd, q1_odd) = src[idx + half + quarter]`\n- Computes polynomial contributions via `accumulate_compute_contributions` (identical to existing kernel)\n- Outputs block sums (identical to existing kernel)\n- Does NOT write to any tree buffer\n\nThis is essentially `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` with the revert logic (lines 466-486) replaced by direct reads, and no writes to the tree buffer.\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void compute_round_from_leaves_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n    const FracExt *__restrict__ src,  // Read-only source (leaf backup)\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n    FpExt lambda,\n    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n) {\n    // Same grid/block/shared as compute_round_and_revert_kernel\n    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n\n    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n    uint32_t idx_base = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n\n    for (uint32_t idx = idx_base; idx < num_x / 2; idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        // Direct reads from backup — NO field inversion\n        auto [p0_even, q0_even] = src[idx];\n        auto [p1_even, q1_even] = src[idx + half];\n        auto [p0_odd, q0_odd] = src[idx + quarter];\n        auto [p1_odd, q1_odd] = src[idx + half + quarter];\n\n        // Polynomial computation (identical to existing kernel)\n        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n            local0, local1\n        );\n    }\n\n    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n}\n```\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI binding and Rust wrapper\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n**What**: Add `extern \"C\"` declaration for `_frac_compute_round_from_leaves` and a safe Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_leaves(eq_buffer, src, num_x, lambda, d_sum_evals, tmp_block_sums)`.\n\n### Change 4: Add launcher in gkr.cu\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n**What**: Add `extern \"C\" int _frac_compute_round_from_leaves(...)` launcher function with same grid/block calculation as the existing `_frac_compute_round_and_revert`.\n\n### Change 5: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves` Rust function\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: New function parallel to `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert` but using `frac_compute_round_from_leaves` instead:\n```rust\nfn do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves<SC, TS>(\n    eq_buffer: &mut SqrtEqLayers,\n    leaf_backup: &DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    pq_size: usize,\n    lambda: EF,\n    transcript: &mut TS,\n    d_sum_evals: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    tmp_block_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    round_polys_eval: &mut Vec<[EF; GKR_S_DEG]>,\n    r_vec: &mut Vec<EF>,\n    prev_s_eval: &mut EF,\n    xi_j: EF,\n    eq_r_acc: &mut EF,\n) -> Result<EF, FractionalSumcheckError>\n```\n\n### Change 6: Replace last outer round's inner round 0 with leaf-based variant\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**Location**: The inner round 0 call at line 698\n**What**: For the LAST outer round only (when `round == total_rounds - 1`), replace `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, ...)` with `do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(&leaf_backup, ...)`.\n\nAfter this, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`, since `layer` was not reverted:\n\n```rust\nif round == total_rounds - 1 {\n    // Last outer round: use backup instead of reverting\n    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_from_leaves(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &leaf_backup, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r0;\n    // First fused round reads from leaf_backup instead of layer\n    // Use BufferScheduler but with initial source = leaf_backup\n    // ... (see below)\n} else {\n    // Other outer rounds: use existing revert path\n    let r0 = do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda, transcript,\n        &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n    )?;\n    prev_r = r0;\n}\n```\n\nFor the last outer round's fused rounds, the FIRST fused round source must be `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`. The `BufferScheduler`'s first target should be `BackupToWork` (read from leaf_backup, fold to work_buffer). Subsequent fused rounds operate normally (work ↔ layer ping-pong).\n\n### Change 7: Adjust BufferScheduler for leaf-backup source\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n**What**: Add a `BackupToWork` variant to `BufferTarget` or handle the first fused round's source specially when the backup path is used. The simplest approach:\n\n```rust\n// For last outer round, first fused inner round:\nlet r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n    &mut eq_buffer,\n    &leaf_backup,  // source: backup instead of layer\n    &mut work_buffer,\n    pq_size,  // src_pq_size (before fold)\n    lambda, prev_r, transcript,\n    &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n    &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval,\n    xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n)?;\nprev_r = r1;\npq_size >>= 1;\n// Subsequent fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\nlet mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\nscheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;  // Override: data is in work_buffer, not layer\n```\n\nThis requires making `data_in_work_buffer` field `pub(super)` or adding a constructor that starts with data in the work buffer.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The compute kernel must produce identical s'(1) and s'(2) values. The only change is HOW the (p0/q0, p1/q1) values are obtained — from backup reads vs. in-place revert — not WHAT values are used.\n2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round after the backup-based compute must fold from backup (which has the same values as the reverted layer would have) to work_buffer using r0. This produces the same folded output.\n3. **Buffer lifecycle**: `leaf_backup` must remain allocated until the last outer round completes. It can be freed after.\n4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged — still use `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert`.\n5. **PrecomputeM strategy**: For the last outer round, if `PrecomputeM` strategy is selected, the backup path must provide the same leaf values to `frac_precompute_m_build_raw` and `frac_multifold_raw`. This may require routing the backup buffer to the PrecomputeM code path. If complex, scope to `FoldEval` strategy only and fall back to revert for PrecomputeM at the last round (conservative approach).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n2. Compare `STARK excl trace` and `LogUp GKR` metrics\n3. Expected: LogUp GKR improves by 15-25ms at APC 300 (50% of revert kernel time for last outer round)\n4. Expected: No regression at APC 0 (similar benefit but ~5 segments, so total savings ~5ms/seg)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms\n- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n"}}
