{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sn8VLR1V8GVzT175s7gtBK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0600-eliminate-gkr-revert-field-inversions\n2\t\n3\tReplace the `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` in GKR fractional sumcheck inner round 0 with a read-only kernel that reads pre-tree-build leaf values from a backup buffer, eliminating the expensive `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversions (one FpExt `inv()` per element). The revert currently performs ~44 Fp multiplications per element (tower-based FpExt reciprocal) to recover the un-combined leaf values from the in-place-built tree. By copying the leaf buffer before the final tree layer is built (~4 MB D2D copy at APC 300), inner round 0 can read the original values directly without field inversions. The `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` accounts for 70ms total across the proof (141 instances) and the revert's field inversions are the dominant per-element cost.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1pc1scBgzkR6RxM75HddD","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"70c72ee0-c920-4d35-b179-ca4f8abed801","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:12:54.093Z"}
