{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0153JorwgtjZGdHx6xWZnLFN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Eliminate GKR Revert Field Inversions (v2)\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate the `frac_unadd_inplace` field inversion writes in `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` for the GKR fractional sumcheck's last outer round by providing a pre-tree-build backup of leaf values. The revert currently writes recovered (un-combined) values back to the tree buffer (64 bytes per element); by reading originals from a backup instead, we eliminate both the `inv()` compute and the write-back traffic. At APC 300, the last outer round processes ~N/2 elements (the largest instance), and the write-back bandwidth dominates small-to-medium tree sizes.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Tree building (`fractional.rs:525-576`)\n10\t1. `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2(buf, total_rounds, alpha)` — atomically fuses: (a) bit-reversal permutation, (b) alpha addition to ALL denominators (`q += alpha`), (c) tree layers 0+1 build via `frac_add_inplace`. Modifies buffer in-place.\n11\t2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers` loop — builds remaining layers in pairs.\n12\t3. `frac_build_tree_layer` — optional single remaining layer.\n13\t4. Root extraction + revert (line 581).\n14\t\n15\t### Sumcheck inner round 0 (`fractional.rs:695-711`)\n16\tFor each outer round `r`:\n17\t- `do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(&mut layer, pq_size, ...)` calls `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` (gkr.cu:437)\n18\t- The kernel reads `lhs = layer[idx]` (combined) and `rhs = layer[idx+half]` (preserved)\n19\t- Computes `inv(rhs.q)`, recovers original lhs, WRITES reverted value back to `layer[idx]`\n20\t- Computes polynomial contributions from recovered values\n21\t\n22\t### Key problem with v1\n23\tThe v1 plan proposed saving a backup BEFORE `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2`. This is wrong because the kernel fuses bit-reversal + alpha addition + 2 tree layers atomically. A pre-kernel backup has natural-order, no-alpha values — not the bit-reversed, alpha-applied leaves the revert recovers.\n24\t\n25\t## Changes (v2)\n26\t\n27\t### Change 1: Split the fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` for the large-N path\n28\t\n29\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n30\t**Location**: Lines 525-532 (the `if total_leaves > 1024` branch)\n31\t**What**: Replace the single fused `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2` call with separate operations:\n32\t\n33\t```rust\n34\tlet start_layer_i = if total_leaves > 1024 {\n35\t    // Step 1: Bit-reverse permutation\n36\t    unsafe {\n37\t        let buf = transmute::<&DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &DeviceBuffer<(EF, EF)>>(&layer);\n38\t        bit_rev_frac_ext(buf, buf, total_rounds as u32, total_leaves as u32, 1)\n39\t            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::BitReversal)?;\n40\t    }\n41\t    // Step 2: Add alpha to all denominators\n42\t    unsafe {\n43\t        frac_add_alpha_all(&layer, alpha)\n44\t            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n45\t    }\n46\t    // Step 3: Save backup of post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree-build leaves\n47\t    let leaf_backup = layer.clone_to_new_buffer()?;\n48\t    // Step 4: Build tree layers 0+1\n49\t    unsafe {\n50\t        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n51\t            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n52\t        frac_build_tree_layer(&mut layer, total_leaves >> 1, false, EF::ZERO, false)\n53\t            .map_err(FractionalSumcheckError::SegmentTree)?;\n54\t    }\n55\t    2\n56\t} else {\n57\t    // Small-N path unchanged — also save backup here\n58\t    // ... (add backup after bitrev + alpha, before tree build)\n59\t};\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t**New kernel needed**: `frac_add_alpha_all` — adds `alpha` to the `.q` field of ALL FracExt elements (not just the second half as the existing `frac_add_alpha` does). This is a simple element-wise kernel.\n63\t\n64\t**Performance impact of splitting**: The fused kernel saved ~1.5N global memory reads. Splitting adds ~1.5N reads back. For N = 2^21 = 2M elements: 2M × 32 bytes × 1.5 = 96 MB extra reads per call, at 1000 GB/s = 0.096ms per call. With ~6 calls: 0.58ms total overhead. Negligible vs expected savings.\n65\t\n66\t### Change 2: Add `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` CUDA kernel\n67\t\n68\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu`\n69\t**What**: A read-only variant of `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` that reads from a separate backup buffer:\n70\t\n71\t```cuda\n72\t__global__ void compute_round_from_backup_kernel(\n73\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_low,\n74\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_xi_high,\n75\t    const FracExt *__restrict__ backup,  // Read-only: post-bitrev, post-alpha, pre-tree leaves\n76\t    uint32_t num_x,\n77\t    uint32_t log_eq_low_cap,\n78\t    FpExt lambda,\n79\t    FpExt *__restrict__ block_sums\n80\t) {\n81\t    extern __shared__ FpExt shared[];\n82\t    const uint32_t half = num_x;\n83\t    const uint32_t quarter = num_x >> 1;\n84\t    FpExt local0 = FpExt(Fp::zero()), local1 = FpExt(Fp::zero());\n85\t\n86\t    for (uint32_t idx = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n87\t         idx < num_x / 2;\n88\t         idx += blockDim.x * gridDim.x)\n89\t    {\n90\t        // Direct reads from backup — NO inv(), NO writes\n91\t        FpExt p0_even = backup[idx].p,       q0_even = backup[idx].q;\n92\t        FpExt p1_even = backup[idx+half].p,   q1_even = backup[idx+half].q;\n93\t        FpExt p0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].p, q0_odd  = backup[idx+quarter].q;\n94\t        FpExt p1_odd  = backup[idx+half+quarter].p, q1_odd = backup[idx+half+quarter].q;\n95\t\n96\t        accumulate_compute_contributions(\n97\t            eq_xi_low, eq_xi_high, idx, log_eq_low_cap, lambda,\n98\t            p0_even, q0_even, p0_odd, q0_odd,\n99\t            p1_even, q1_even, p1_odd, q1_odd,\n100\t            local0, local1\n101\t        );\n102\t    }\n103\t    reduce_block_sums(shared, local0, local1, block_sums);\n104\t}\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\t**Key differences from `compute_round_and_revert_kernel`**:\n108\t- Reads from `backup` (const), not `layer` (mutable)\n109\t- No `inv(rhs.q)` call — reads original values directly\n110\t- No writes to tree buffer — eliminates 64 bytes/element write traffic\n111\t- Read traffic reduced from 128 bytes (4 FracExt from tree) to 128 bytes (4 FracExt from backup) — same read volume but no writes\n112\t\n113\t### Change 3: Add FFI bindings and launcher\n114\t\n115\t**Files**: `gkr.cu` (launcher), `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (FFI binding)\n116\t**What**: Launcher `_frac_compute_round_from_backup(eq_low, eq_high, backup, num_x, eq_low_cap, lambda, out, tmp_block_sums)` and Rust wrapper `frac_compute_round_from_backup(...)`.\n117\t\n118\t### Change 4: Add `do_sumcheck_round_from_backup` Rust function\n119\t\n120\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n121\t**What**: New function that calls `frac_compute_round_from_backup` instead of `frac_compute_round_and_revert`, then delegates to `observe_and_update` (same as existing).\n122\t\n123\t### Change 5: Use backup path for the last outer round\n124\t\n125\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n126\t**Location**: Inner round 0 dispatch (~line 698)\n127\t**What**: When `round == total_rounds - 1` (last outer round):\n128\t\n129\t```rust\n130\tlet r0 = if round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n131\t    do_sumcheck_round_from_backup(\n132\t        &mut eq_buffer, leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap(), pq_size, lambda,\n133\t        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n134\t        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n135\t    )?\n136\t} else {\n137\t    do_sumcheck_round_and_revert(\n138\t        &mut eq_buffer, &mut layer, pq_size, lambda,\n139\t        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n140\t        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[0], &mut eq_r_acc,\n141\t    )?\n142\t};\n143\t```\n144\t\n145\t### Change 6: Route first fused round to read from backup\n146\t\n147\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n148\t**What**: For the last outer round, the first fused inner round (round 1) must read from `leaf_backup` instead of `layer`:\n149\t\n150\t```rust\n151\t// For last outer round: first fused round reads from backup\n152\tif round == total_rounds - 1 && leaf_backup.is_some() {\n153\t    let backup = leaf_backup.as_ref().unwrap();\n154\t    let r1 = do_fused_sumcheck_round(\n155\t        &mut eq_buffer, backup, &mut work_buffer, pq_size, lambda, prev_r,\n156\t        transcript, &mut d_sum_evals, &mut tmp_block_sums,\n157\t        &mut round_polys_eval, &mut r_vec, &mut prev_s_eval, xi_prev[1], &mut eq_r_acc,\n158\t    )?;\n159\t    prev_r = r1;\n160\t    pq_size >>= 1;\n161\t\n162\t    // Remaining fused rounds: scheduler starts with data in work_buffer\n163\t    let mut scheduler = BufferScheduler::new(max_work_size);\n164\t    scheduler.data_in_work_buffer = true;\n165\t    for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(2) {\n166\t        // ... normal fused rounds with scheduler\n167\t    }\n168\t} else {\n169\t    // ... existing non-backup path\n170\t}\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\t### Change 7: Handle PrecomputeM strategy\n174\t\n175\tFor the last outer round with `PrecomputeM` strategy, fall back to the existing revert path. This is the conservative approach:\n176\t\n177\t```rust\n178\tlet use_backup = round == total_rounds - 1\n179\t    && leaf_backup.is_some()\n180\t    && matches!(backend, GkrRoundStrategy::FoldEval);\n181\t```\n182\t\n183\t## Invariants\n184\t\n185\t1. **Polynomial evaluation correctness**: The backup buffer contains exactly the pre-tree-build, post-bitrev, post-alpha leaf values. At the last outer round, these are the values that `compute_round_and_revert` would recover via `frac_unadd`. Reading them directly produces identical `(p0_even, q0_even, p1_even, q1_even, p0_odd, q0_odd, p1_odd, q1_odd)` values.\n186\t2. **Fold correctness**: The first fused round reads from `leaf_backup` (same data as the reverted layer would contain) and folds with `r0`. Subsequent rounds fold from work_buffer/layer normally.\n187\t3. **Alpha application**: The backup has alpha already applied to all denominators (from the explicit `frac_add_alpha_all` step). This matches the post-bitrev-pre-tree state.\n188\t4. **Non-last outer rounds**: Completely unchanged.\n189\t5. **PrecomputeM fallback**: Last outer round with PrecomputeM uses the existing revert path.\n190\t6. **Memory**: The backup buffer uses N FracExt elements of extra GPU memory. At APC 300 with N ≈ 2M: ~64 MB. Within budget.\n191\t7. **Small-N fallback**: For total_leaves ≤ 1024, the code already uses separate bitrev + tree build. The backup can be inserted similarly.\n192\t\n193\t## Measurement Plan\n194\t\n195\t1. Run `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300\n196\t2. Compare `LogUp GKR`, `STARK excl trace` metrics\n197\t3. Use nsight to verify `compute_round_and_revert_kernel` instance count decreases (replaced by `compute_round_from_backup_kernel` for last outer round)\n198\t4. Expected: ~5-15ms improvement on STARK excl trace at APC 300 (from eliminating revert writes and inv() compute for the largest tree level)\n199\t5. Expected: No regression at APC 0\n200\t\n201\t## Rollback Criteria\n202\t\n203\t- Revert if STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 5ms\n204\t- Revert if any APC configuration shows regression > 20ms\n205\t- Revert if any correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n206\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1pc1scBgzkR6RxM75HddD","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"e9a9df96-9383-41ad-b40c-61ed2b30aa93","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:12:54.622Z"}
