{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HJ2GjcB4JyQWxz8HYkHb1T","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0600-preallocate-whir-buffers-early\n2\t\n3\tPre-allocate WHIR's key device buffers (f_ple_evals, f_coeffs, w_moments) at the start of the STARK proving phase, before the Trace Commit and Constraints phases allocate their temporary buffers. The WHIR phase regressed 28ms (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) after the VPMM page size increase from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The regression was attributed to VPMM pool state changes affecting WHIR's bandwidth-bound kernels. By pre-allocating WHIR buffers early (before pool fragmentation from intermediate phases), the buffers may get more favorable physical memory placement, restoring bandwidth characteristics closer to the baseline.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUHyPperqMPJvJQAc3D3Rh","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"20fa28ae-8146-423f-a0e0-f6edd458e9e5","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:26:18.647Z"}
