{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Dpkus6P2Y9tSSgcuAKDFzv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012fSXcxbakfB67pyrK3N3uy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n\nTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_read_input_tokens":322817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"462fc571-209f-457b-b635-2bb1ccba591b"}
