{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TEVT4VrTFjL5FgGD9jHnHF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n2\t\n3\tTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J17JjUQ3eVEaLrWxZRQ1KK","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"bd0f0b6d-047d-43d9-a1b1-47fe720c640b","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:35:26.495Z"}
