{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017jP8x5UDnKhLm5FGfmBy5j","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Decouple VPMM Pool Threshold from Page Size\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tIntroduce a configurable `pool_threshold` parameter that determines the minimum allocation size routed to the VPMM virtual-memory system, independent of the physical `page_size`. By raising this threshold from 16 MiB (current page_size) to 64 MiB, allocations in the 16–64 MiB range will use `cudaMallocAsync` instead of the VPMM, avoiding per-allocation `cuMemCreate` calls, page tracking, and defragmentation overhead. The page_size remains at 16 MiB for large VPMM allocations.\n6\t\n7\tThis follows the pattern established by the `vpmm-bulk-page-creation` task, which showed that routing medium-sized allocations (2–16 MiB) through `cudaMallocAsync` instead of VPMM gave −136 ms on LogUp GKR + Constraints at APC 300 — far beyond the expected savings from reduced `cuMemCreate` calls alone.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Allocation routing (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:71-92`)\n12\t\n13\t```rust\n14\tfn d_malloc(&mut self, size: usize) -> Result<*mut c_void, MemoryError> {\n15\t    let mut tracked_size = size;\n16\t    let ptr = if size < self.pool.page_size {     // ← threshold = page_size\n17\t        // cudaMallocAsync path\n18\t        cudaMallocAsync(&mut ptr, size, cudaStreamPerThread);\n19\t        self.allocated_ptrs.insert(ptr, size);\n20\t        ptr\n21\t    } else {\n22\t        // VPMM path\n23\t        tracked_size = size.next_multiple_of(self.pool.page_size);\n24\t        self.pool.malloc_internal(tracked_size, stream_id)?\n25\t    };\n26\t    // ...\n27\t}\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\t### Deallocation routing (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:104-119`)\n31\t\n32\t```rust\n33\tunsafe fn d_free(&mut self, ptr: *mut c_void) -> Result<(), MemoryError> {\n34\t    if let Some(size) = self.allocated_ptrs.remove(&nn) {\n35\t        // cudaMallocAsync path — ptr was in allocated_ptrs\n36\t        cudaFreeAsync(ptr, cudaStreamPerThread);\n37\t    } else {\n38\t        // VPMM path — ptr was in pool.malloc_regions\n39\t        self.pool.free_internal(ptr, stream_id)?;\n40\t    }\n41\t}\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tThe deallocation path is routing-agnostic: it checks `allocated_ptrs` first, falls through to VPMM. No change needed here.\n45\t\n46\t### Configuration (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/vm_pool.rs:35-86`)\n47\t\n48\t`VpmmConfig` has fields `page_size`, `va_size`, `initial_pages`. It loads from environment variables in `from_env()`. `VirtualMemoryPool` stores `page_size` at field `vm_pool.rs:134`.\n49\t\n50\t### Key allocations in the 16–64 MiB range"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J17JjUQ3eVEaLrWxZRQ1KK","session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"ecec5eea-8fbe-4a50-8fac-c492062bab15","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:35:45.455Z"}
