{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163XbeEWieZMEWcAWgYHc3z","type":"tool_result","content":"=== Checklist ===\n1. autoopt/autoopt_context.md read: YES\n2. autoopt/context.md read: YES\n3. log.md and reports read: YES (43 entries, 43 reports)\n4. Baseline exists:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 2092817 Apr 12 21:20 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/baseline/apc300.json\n5. Current performance measured:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 2092794 Apr 16 01:35 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n6. Profiling done: YES (nsight kernel summary analyzed)\n7. Multiple ideas generated and ranked: YES (5 ideas)\n8. task.md:\n# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n\nTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n9. plan.md:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 5075 Apr 16 06:35 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir/plan.md\n10. Review: Approved (no design-level blockers, prototype-ready)\n11. Source code NOT modified:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80cd739d-0408-463a-95a7-972cb66aaf37","uuid":"b32dfc3b-c7e2-4c25-812a-eae6c8b3993a","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:37:36.876Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== Checklist ===\n1. autoopt/autoopt_context.md read: YES\n2. autoopt/context.md read: YES\n3. log.md and reports read: YES (43 entries, 43 reports)\n4. Baseline exists:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 2092817 Apr 12 21:20 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/baseline/apc300.json\n5. Current performance measured:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 2092794 Apr 16 01:35 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n6. Profiling done: YES (nsight kernel summary analyzed)\n7. Multiple ideas generated and ranked: YES (5 ideas)\n8. task.md:\n# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n\nTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n9. plan.md:\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 5075 Apr 16 06:35 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir/plan.md\n10. Review: Approved (no design-level blockers, prototype-ready)\n11. Source code NOT modified:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
